  "summary": "The Just Security litigation tracker showed 900 cases on July 16, 2026 (question publication). Resolution is August 31, 2026, ~46 days later. The clean 2026 series (627 Feb 10 → 753 Apr 9 → 900 Jul 16) implies a recent growth rate of ~1.5 cases/day (earlier 2026 was ~2.17/day). Extrapolating 1.5/day over 46 days gives ~+69 → ~969. A scenario mixture (70% steady 1.5/day, 15% acceleration 2.3/day, 15% deceleration/consolidation 0.6/day, plus a 5% methodology recalibration jump reflecting the prior 708→627 recalibration) yields a median of ~969 with P10 931 / P90 1005. The lower bound 899.5 sits at the current level (unlikely to fall below barring consolidation); the upper bound 1099.5 is essentially unreachable at current rates (would require ~4.3/day).",
  "reasoning": "Forecast submitted.\n\n**Summary:** The Just Security tracker showed **900 lawsuits** on July 16, 2026 (question publication date). With ~46 days until the August 31 resolution and a recent growth rate of ~1.5 cases/day (from the clean 2026 series: 627 → 753 → 900), the extrapolated median is **~969 lawsuits**.\n\n**Distribution:**\n- P10: 931\n- P50: 969\n- P90: 1005\n\nThe forecast centers on the recent steady rate but widens both tails via a scenario mixture accounting for possible acceleration (litigation bursts from new executive actions, as seen in early 2026 at 2.17/day) and deceleration/consolidation risk (the tracker was previously recalibrated from ~708 to 627). The creator's lower bound of 899.5 sits right at the current level, and the upper bound of 1099.5 would require an implausible ~4.3 cases/day.",
